==English==
{{wikipedia|ollie (skateboarding)|Ollie}}

===Etymology===
From “Ollie”, the nickname of the Florida skateboarder [[w:Alan Gelfand|Alan Gelfand]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|skateboarding|surfing|snowboarding}} An aerial maneuver in which one [[catch air|catches air]] by leaping off the ground with the skateboard and into the air.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|ollies|ollying|pres_ptc2=ollieing|ollied}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To perform an ollie.
#* {{quote-book|year=1992|title=Mean Street  |author=Troy Bannon  |page=41 |ISBN=0440405882 |passage=He used the tilted side as a ramp, grabbed some air, fakied down, and '''ollied''' back onto level ground. }}

